{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to run an OCI-containerized web application on port 8080 as the unprivileged nologin account appsvc. The service is enabled at boot, operates without an appsvc login session, and recovered successfully after a verified node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed runc and created a minimal read-only container root filesystem.","Created appsvc as an unprivileged system account with /usr/sbin/nologin.","Created and enabled rootless-web.service under systemd.","Verified HTTP service, container ownership, UID/GID mappings, namespace isolation, and zero appsvc login sessions.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified its boot identity changed and the application recovered automatically."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Containerized web application runs as unprivileged appsvc on port 8080 without an active login session","command_ids":["cmd-f76a760721344c0a","cmd-a1b22bea4dde4c5f"],"summary":"HTTP returned the expected page on port 8080. runc reported owner appsvc; the process ran as UID 112; UID/GID maps mapped container root to appsvc; PID and mount namespaces differed from the host; appsvc had zero login sessions and a nologin shell."},{"requirement":"Application starts automatically at boot","command_ids":["cmd-aeeed38bdc584dbf","cmd-a1b22bea4dde4c5f"],"summary":"rootless-web.service was enabled and active before reboot, then automatically became active after reboot with a newly created container and successful HTTP response."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f76a760721344c0a","cmd-5f9d208857b34636","cmd-f4916fe1333549b0","cmd-a1b22bea4dde4c5f"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID fa1e87e6-00f3-42d2-acc5-ad1df6c3d16a; reboot scheduling was acknowledged; post-reboot boot ID changed to 12364f73-2cd3-4d3b-ad50-5c2e02dce97c; system state, service, container, listener, application data, ownership, isolation, and no-login operation all recovered."}]}
